          "text": "CLINICAL INDICATION  \nHistory of drug-resistant combined generalized and focal epilepsy of unknown etiology, with focal impaired awareness seizures beginning at age 27 and occurring approximately once per month. Current antiseizure medications are zonisamide, lacosamide, and perampanel.\n\nTECHNIQUE  \nRoutine digital scalp EEG was recorded using electrodes placed according to the International 10–20 system.\n\nFINDINGS  \nInterictal epileptiform abnormalities are present in both generalized and focal distributions. No further focal localization or ictal localization is assigned from this recording.\n\nIMPRESSION  \nAbnormal routine EEG demonstrating combined generalized and focal epileptiform activity. These findings are compatible with the reported epilepsy classification in the appropriate clinical context; EEG findings alone do not determine the clinical seizure type or establish an ictal onset location.",
